# Rise from the Wreck's "up to one target creature card with no abilities" still finds a vanilla creature card beside permanents
# that only could give it a way to be cast: Lurrus of the Dream-Den's "you may cast a permanent spell with mana value 2 or less
# from your graveyard" is Lurrus's permission, no ability of the card (CR 113.6, 601.3), and Ninja Teen below level 3 gives
# graveyard creature cards no sneak yet. Turn 1: Ninja Teen and Lurrus. Turn 3: Grizzly Bears is cast and Lightning Bolted.
# Turn 5, with Lurrus's permission unused: Rise takes the Bears both for "target creature card" and for the no-abilities slot
# (one card for two targets, CR 115.3), and it returns once.

